{
  "title": "Namaz for Fulfillment of Needs (3)",
  "data": "After the taslim and the glorification (tasbih), recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) fifty-one times, and then say each of the following fifty times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ\nASTAGHFIRULLAAH\nI seek forgiveness of Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.\nلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nThere is no might and no strength save in Allah, the High, the Great.\nThen say the following supplication:\nيَا اَللّٰهُ الْمَانِعُ قُدْرَتَهٗ خَلْقَهٗ\nYAA ALLAAHUL MAANI'U QUDRATAHOO KHALQAH\nO Allah, Who withholds His power from His creatures,\nوَالْمَالِكُ بِهَا سُلْطَانَهٗ\nWAL MAALIKU BIHAA SULTAANAH\nand through it holds His dominion,\nوَالْمُتَسَلِّطُ بِمَا فِيْ يَدَيْهِ عَلٰى كُلِّ مَوْجُوْدٍ\nWAL MUTASALLITU BIMAA FEE YADAYHI A'LAA KULLI MAWJOOD\nand by what is in His hands has authority over everything that exists!\nوَغَيْرُكَ يَخِيْبُ رَجَآءُ رَاجِيْهِ\nWA GHAYRUKA YAKHEEBU RAJAA'U RAAJEEH\nWhoever hopes in other than You is disappointed in his hope,\nوَرَاجِيْكَ مَسْرُوْرٌ لَا يَخِيْبُ\nWA RAAJEEKA MASROORUN LAA YAKHEEB\nbut whoever hopes in You is gladdened and never disappointed.\nاَسْئَلُكَ بِكُلِّ رِضًى لَكَ\nAS'ALUKA BIKULLI RIDAN LAK\nI ask You by everything that pleases You,\nوَبِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ اَنْتَ فِيْهِ\nWA BIKULLI SHAY'IN ANTA FEEH\nby everything in which You are,\nوَبِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ تُحِبُّ اَنْ تُذْكَرَ بِهٖ\nWA BIKULLI SHAY'IN TUHIBBU AN TUDHKARA BIH\nby everything by which You love to be remembered,\nوَبِكَ يَا اَللّٰهُ فَلَيْسَ يَعْدِلُكَ شَيْءٌ\nWA BIKA YAA ALLAAHU FALAYSA YA'DILUKA SHAY'\nand by You, O Allah, for nothing is equal to You,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nto send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَتَحْفَظَنِيْ وَوَلَدِيْ وَاَهْلِيْ وَمَالِيْ\nWA TAHFAZANEE WA WALADEE WA AHLEE WA MAALEE\nto safeguard me, my children, my family and my property,\nوَتَحْفَظَنِيْ بِحِفْظِكَ\nWA TAHFAZANEE BIHIFZIK\nto guard me with Your guarding,\nوَاَنْ تَقْضِيَ حَاجَتِيْ فِيْ كَذَا وَكَذَا\nWA AN TAQDIYA HAAJATEE FEE KADHAA WA KADHAA\nand to settle my need concerning such-and-such.\nMention your need in place of \"such-and-such\".",
  "merits": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus, in his book of al-Mazar (chapter: Rites of al-Kufah Mosque), after mentioning the recommended acts at Imam Ali (a.s.)'s niche (mihrab), has mentioned a special prayer for settling the needs to be offered there.\nIt consists of four units, each two alone (the taslim is said after every two units). In the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) ten times; in the second, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) twenty-one times; in the third, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) thirty-one times; and in the fourth, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) forty-one times."
}
